    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3154dd6_e89d8895",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ascp/mem_map.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 4405694
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T11:01:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Data in flash is persistent, in RAM it is generated once per runtime during the boot. Nothing is written later. I do not see how cashing could be a problem here.",
      "parentUuid": "cd440870_e1bf69e8",
      "revId": "d81c9ca4b5c2fee92f4409bb50b4810df2ae898a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c760faa_f445ecda",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ascp/mem_map.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-03T12:25:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My consideration was that some hw engine like SHA256 or DMA (controlled by bootloader) writes to the RAM and the cache is marked as valid for some reason. But I think it such case, this memory should be marked ad non-cacheable in dts per project so I think we are fine.",
      "parentUuid": "a3154dd6_e89d8895",
      "revId": "d81c9ca4b5c2fee92f4409bb50b4810df2ae898a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
